v0.4 (major modernization)
install latest 3x-ui dynamically (v3.11.0+ with Xray-core 26.x) instead of pinned v2.9.4
Hysteria2 inbound created by default: native 3x-ui hysteria inbound (version 2, UDP),
  TLS alpn h3, salamander obfs via finalmask (RU DPI resistance), masquerade serves the fake site over HTTP/3
  (clients land in the normalized tables clients + client_inbounds, which v3 builds the running config from)
WARP for all inbound connections: WARP device registered via api.cloudflareclient.com,
  warp wireguard outbound installed as the FIRST (default) outbound in xrayTemplateConfig;
  credentials stored in the panel DB so the panel WARP UI keeps working; end-to-end egress verified
xhttp modernized: gRPC/UDS socket replaced with TCP inbound behind nginx proxy_pass HTTP/1.1;
  mode auto, noGRPCHeader, xPaddingBytes 100-1000
trojan migrated from deprecated gRPC transport to XHTTP (same modern schema)
masquerade (web-camouflage) page now sourced from the git_land directory (git-login-y2k.html),
  with raw.githubusercontent fallback for remote installs (no more random fake sites)
idempotent reinstall: settings/inbounds/clients are cleaned before insert (no duplicate keys)
ufw: allow 443/udp and the Hysteria2 UDP port
repo cleanup: moved to github.com/bvrbedwire/unknxwn (project renamed to "unknow"); all remote
  URLs (sub pages, clash configs, git_land masquerade) now point to this repo; the main
  script is now unknow.sh; removed outdated files (x-ui-latest.sh, randomfakehtml.sh,
  repare-after-286-update.sh) and the stale media/ screenshots; README rewritten to
  match the current configuration
